WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.260
- All right, so imagine this.

00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:04.470
You're creating a new
startup smartphone company.

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:07.020
Your goal, of course, is
to make it huge, right?

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:10.110
So you make your first phone,
you launch with a bang,

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:11.910
you've got a bunch of
enthusiasts on board,

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:13.770
and you're slowly starting
to grow this thing.

00:00:13.770 --> 00:00:17.130
And it starts going well
in Europe and in India

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:18.840
and a few other Asian markets,

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:21.210
and, you know, things are starting to grow

00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:23.130
and go quite nicely.

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:25.800
But you notice there's not a lot of pickup

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:27.720
in the United States for some reason.

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:30.270
Now, there's a few
reasons why this might be.

00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:31.560
I mean, a lot of people already know

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:33.720
there's a surprisingly
high amount of people

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:35.790
who just walk into a carrier store

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:37.110
to buy their phones in the US,

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:39.900
so if you don't have
a deal with a carrier,

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:42.330
then things might not
go well for you there.

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:44.580
And this is a enthusiast-only thing.

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:47.670
They're selling them online,
so that's understandable.

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:50.730
But then you get to the stats,

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:52.890
and the stats say the iPhone

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:56.850
has somewhere around 50%
market share in the US,

00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:58.410
which is higher than the global average,

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:01.920
and it is steadily
growing every single year.

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:06.240
And worst of all, 87%, that's not a typo,

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:09.930
87% of teenagers in the US have an iPhone.

00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:14.010
And that honestly feels
like the most damning one

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:16.140
because that means they got them early.

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:17.940
Like, everyone knows about the walls

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:19.710
Apple builds up around their ecosystem

00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:23.340
to try to keep people in
the iPhone walled garden.

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:26.460
But 87% of teenagers, that just means

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:28.440
that this is a lot of these
people's first phones.

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:31.860
These people will be iPhone
customers for life maybe.

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:34.380
Like, for a lot of them, their
friends all have iPhones,

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:36.390
and if they're gonna get their first phone

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:37.223
for the first time,

00:01:37.223 --> 00:01:39.390
they don't really even consider anything

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:41.280
that isn't also an iPhone.

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:42.780
It's the only way to get
into all the group chats

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:43.613
with their friends.

00:01:43.613 --> 00:01:45.570
It's the only way to get
in on all the inside jokes

00:01:45.570 --> 00:01:48.180
and socializations that
happen after school

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:50.370
from the FaceTimes to the iMessages

00:01:50.370 --> 00:01:52.320
and all the things that
are just iPhone only.

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:54.930
So it's a very baked-in thing.

00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:57.930
It's a very US-centric thing for sure,

00:01:57.930 --> 00:01:59.010
but it is everywhere.

00:01:59.010 --> 00:02:00.210
So this is why, when I made

00:02:00.210 --> 00:02:03.030
that "Blue Bubbles vs. Green
Bubbles: Explained!" video,

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:04.680
I had to put that disclaimer
in the beginning of the video,

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:06.457
but that's why half
the comments were like,

00:02:06.457 --> 00:02:09.030
"Yeah, I live in the US,
and I see this everywhere.

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:10.380
There's iPhones everywhere,

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:13.080
and the pressure of the
iPhone is very real."

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:15.487
And then the other half
of the comments are like,

00:02:15.487 --> 00:02:18.030
"This is the dumbest thing I've ever seen.

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:20.850
Why do people care so much
about which phone people use?

00:02:20.850 --> 00:02:23.790
Just use WhatsApp. It's super easy."

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:25.470
And so that's why that dichotomy exists.

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:26.310
But, you know, you get the idea.

00:02:26.310 --> 00:02:28.170
So you are that smartphone company.

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:29.430
You're in this position.

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:31.530
You're trying to break out in the US.

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:32.523
What do you do?

00:02:33.390 --> 00:02:34.530
It's a real question,

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:37.170
and as some of you may have picked up

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:39.270
by the title and premise of this video,

00:02:39.270 --> 00:02:40.920
it's a real company too.

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:41.820
It's Nothing.

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:44.610
This is a company that's made
their first two phones now,

00:02:44.610 --> 00:02:46.860
they've got some accessories,
they're trying to break out,

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:51.860
and their options seem to
be just give up on the US

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:54.690
or maybe try to strike a carrier
deal and get in that way,

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:56.880
but it doesn't seem like it might work,

00:02:56.880 --> 00:03:00.660
or just lean all the way in

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:03.960
and embrace the actual
heart of the question,

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:08.070
the number one problem, the
biggest asset of the other side.

00:03:08.070 --> 00:03:09.210
And that's what they're doing.

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:10.830
So what Nothing has decided to do,

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:12.450
and they're announcing this today,

00:03:12.450 --> 00:03:17.450
is they have built iMessage
into their Android phone,

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:21.383
kind of.

00:03:21.383 --> 00:03:23.700
So they've announced a new
app that is gonna come out

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:27.720
and be exclusive to the
Nothing Phone 2 to start,

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:30.360
and it's called the Nothing Chats app.

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:34.380
And their goal with this is
to literally offer iMessage

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:36.660
also on their phone.

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:38.850
Now, how does this work,
you might be asking?

00:03:38.850 --> 00:03:39.990
Great question. Glad you asked.

00:03:39.990 --> 00:03:40.823
So I've got it here.

00:03:40.823 --> 00:03:42.090
This is an app that's co-developed

00:03:42.090 --> 00:03:43.650
with a company called Sunbird

00:03:43.650 --> 00:03:45.030
who has been doing this for a little while

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:46.590
in a restricted beta.

00:03:46.590 --> 00:03:47.550
You might've heard of it,

00:03:47.550 --> 00:03:48.720
and there's also a couple of others

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:50.160
floating around like this.

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:50.993
And basically what it does

00:03:50.993 --> 00:03:53.730
is it lets you sign into
it using an Apple ID.

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:55.500
So you can just sign
up for an Apple account

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:56.760
without any Apple products.

00:03:56.760 --> 00:03:59.670
You sign up for an Apple ID,
and then you sign into the app,

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:03.180
and it will give you as many
iMessage features as possible

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:05.040
without actually having an iPhone.

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:07.410
So, okay, a couple of things about this.

00:04:07.410 --> 00:04:11.010
One, this Nothing Chats
app, when you first sign in,

00:04:11.010 --> 00:04:12.480
is pretty intuitive.

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:15.600
You go through the setup process
to create a Nothing account

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:17.940
and then connect your Apple ID.

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:19.890
So, like I said, you can make an Apple ID

00:04:19.890 --> 00:04:22.170
even if you have no Apple products,

00:04:22.170 --> 00:04:23.370
and then you sign in,

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:25.560
and then everything
just seems to work fine.

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:29.010
It's more or less looking
exactly like a skinned version

00:04:29.010 --> 00:04:30.780
of the Sunbird beta app.

00:04:30.780 --> 00:04:33.600
And so sure enough, when
you go to message an iPhone

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:36.840
or join any group chat that
has a bunch of iPhones in it,

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:40.020
things that would not work
with an Android phone before,

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:41.070
it basically starts off

00:04:41.070 --> 00:04:43.080
by sending through a virtual contact card

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:45.060
asking to merge your contact info

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:46.920
with your Apple ID email address,

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:48.630
and then suddenly it all works,

00:04:48.630 --> 00:04:49.710
and you're a blue bubble,

00:04:49.710 --> 00:04:51.540
and you're texting people with iMessage

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:53.460
from your Android phone.

00:04:53.460 --> 00:04:55.770
Also, high-quality media is working.

00:04:55.770 --> 00:04:56.970
So you might have heard
of this issue already.

00:04:56.970 --> 00:04:58.740
This is actually one of
my biggest annoyances,

00:04:58.740 --> 00:05:00.060
but when you message an iPhone

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:02.310
with an Android phone or vice versa,

00:05:02.310 --> 00:05:03.930
and you send, like, a video or a photo,

00:05:03.930 --> 00:05:04.980
it's, like, super blurry

00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:07.680
because it's been compressed a lot

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:09.930
to fit in the file size limits of MMS.

00:05:09.930 --> 00:05:11.160
But now you actually get

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:13.350
that full-resolution
photo and video treatment

00:05:13.350 --> 00:05:15.720
as if you're just two iPhones
talking to each other,

00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:18.030
which is actually very convenient.

00:05:18.030 --> 00:05:19.440
Typing indicators work

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:21.510
when another person has
been typing for a while,

00:05:21.510 --> 00:05:23.220
and they're also working
on the reactions as well.

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:24.810
It's not in this beta
that I've been testing,

00:05:24.810 --> 00:05:26.070
but they say they're gonna have that

00:05:26.070 --> 00:05:27.510
around the end of this year.

00:05:27.510 --> 00:05:28.343
But then number two,

00:05:28.343 --> 00:05:29.880
they're saying that they're launching this

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:33.360
as an exclusive app for
the Nothing Phone 2,

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:34.770
so just this phone,

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:37.650
and I imagine future
Nothing phones as well,

00:05:37.650 --> 00:05:40.410
to sort of give people that option

00:05:40.410 --> 00:05:42.300
where if they were gonna buy a new phone,

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:45.630
and they really wanna be
in the iMessage group chats

00:05:45.630 --> 00:05:47.430
and all the iMessage features,

00:05:47.430 --> 00:05:48.960
and they could only buy an iPhone,

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:52.650
they'll at least also have
this phone as an option.

00:05:52.650 --> 00:05:54.570
But then three, this is the big one,

00:05:54.570 --> 00:05:57.540
and I cannot stress this enough,

00:05:57.540 --> 00:06:02.160
this could lead to
enormous security issues.

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:04.410
Signing in with your Apple ID

00:06:04.410 --> 00:06:07.470
onto a device that you don't own

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:09.360
is an enormous security issue,

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:11.100
and it's a huge risk to anyone using it.

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:13.320
Same thing is also true
about Beeper and the others.

00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:14.370
Because the way this one works,

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:15.750
and I've confirmed this with Nothing,

00:06:15.750 --> 00:06:18.750
is when you sign in with an Apple ID,

00:06:18.750 --> 00:06:21.960
it's literally signing in on some Mac Mini

00:06:21.960 --> 00:06:23.760
in a server farm somewhere,

00:06:23.760 --> 00:06:26.160
and that Mac Mini will then
do all of the routing for you

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:27.690
to make this happen.

00:06:27.690 --> 00:06:31.800
You will never see or actually
hold or use that Mac Mini.

00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:35.850
Now, no one else is
supposed to be able to use

00:06:35.850 --> 00:06:38.910
or see that Mac Mini
or your messages on it

00:06:38.910 --> 00:06:40.650
because it's all encrypted,

00:06:40.650 --> 00:06:43.770
but you are still logging
in with your own Apple ID

00:06:43.770 --> 00:06:44.820
on someone else's computer.

00:06:44.820 --> 00:06:45.960
I don't know how else to put that.

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:48.780
Like, that on its face
is a big enough risk

00:06:48.780 --> 00:06:50.640
that many people will
never even wanna try this.

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:52.470
But hey, if you're Nothing,

00:06:52.470 --> 00:06:55.747
well, maybe this is just
enough to be able to say,

00:06:55.747 --> 00:06:59.190
"Hey, we're offering iMessage
on an Android phone."

00:06:59.190 --> 00:07:01.350
Like, this is a young
and crazy enough company

00:07:01.350 --> 00:07:03.810
that they're gonna try stuff like this,

00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:06.720
so maybe people will consider
a Nothing phone in the US

00:07:06.720 --> 00:07:07.950
instead of an iPhone

00:07:07.950 --> 00:07:10.080
that everyone seems to
just choose by default.

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:12.240
I actually talked to Nothing about this

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:14.430
as I was testing it before
this is all going live,

00:07:14.430 --> 00:07:16.747
and I actually asked Carl Pei straight up,

00:07:16.747 --> 00:07:21.747
"What do you think Apple is
going to do or say about this

00:07:21.780 --> 00:07:23.370
once they find out about it?"

00:07:23.370 --> 00:07:25.830
Because as this video goes live,

00:07:25.830 --> 00:07:28.050
Apple's finding out about this.

00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:33.050
And his answer was,
"Honestly, probably nothing."

00:07:33.150 --> 00:07:34.980
But just because there's a weird timeline

00:07:34.980 --> 00:07:36.960
we're living in here in 2023

00:07:36.960 --> 00:07:39.750
where Apple kind of can't
really retaliate publicly

00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:41.280
because they've already been up

00:07:41.280 --> 00:07:43.680
against so much antitrust pressure.

00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:46.230
Everyone already knows
Apple is using iMessage

00:07:46.230 --> 00:07:49.020
and its powers to keep people
from leaving the iPhone,

00:07:49.020 --> 00:07:51.390
but if Apple now, like,
publicly acknowledges this

00:07:51.390 --> 00:07:52.920
as a competitor in the space

00:07:52.920 --> 00:07:55.170
that they've gotta shut
down or something like that,

00:07:55.170 --> 00:07:56.460
it could sort of shine a light on it

00:07:56.460 --> 00:07:58.323
in a way they don't actually want,

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:02.340
so they'll probably just
quietly sweep it under the rug

00:08:02.340 --> 00:08:05.640
and maybe just point
out some security risks

00:08:05.640 --> 00:08:06.780
involved with the whole thing.

00:08:06.780 --> 00:08:08.190
But then, of course, the
other side of the coin

00:08:08.190 --> 00:08:10.380
is if Apple cares so much about security,

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:12.030
then wouldn't they wanna support RCS

00:08:12.030 --> 00:08:14.490
so that the millions of
messages that go back and forth

00:08:14.490 --> 00:08:16.950
between Android phones
and iPhones every day

00:08:16.950 --> 00:08:19.620
won't be unencrypted SMS?

00:08:19.620 --> 00:08:22.650
But that's another story for another day.

00:08:22.650 --> 00:08:24.330
But at the end of the
day, the real question is,

00:08:24.330 --> 00:08:25.740
will it work?

00:08:25.740 --> 00:08:30.000
Will this strategy of
offering some iMessage stuff

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:32.010
on their phone exclusively

00:08:32.010 --> 00:08:35.250
actually work for Nothing
to break out in the US?

00:08:35.250 --> 00:08:38.700
And the fact is there's a
non-zero number of people

00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:40.590
who will be willing to try this,

00:08:40.590 --> 00:08:43.950
to give themselves the
iMessage, the blue bubble life

00:08:43.950 --> 00:08:46.050
while still using a different phone.

00:08:46.050 --> 00:08:47.167
There's probably somebody
out there who's like,

00:08:47.167 --> 00:08:48.480
"I might buy a Nothing phone,

00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:51.150
but, also, all my friends have
iPhones, so I guess I can't."

00:08:51.150 --> 00:08:54.240
And for them, this is real, it's great,

00:08:54.240 --> 00:08:56.490
but there's a lot of baggage with that,

00:08:56.490 --> 00:08:59.520
and it's sort of a weird
timeline we're living in now

00:08:59.520 --> 00:09:02.160
that this is actually a possible
thing that could happen.

00:09:02.160 --> 00:09:03.450
Let me know what your thoughts are

00:09:03.450 --> 00:09:04.710
in the comment section below,

00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:06.510
if you think this will work.

00:09:06.510 --> 00:09:08.010
Thanks for watching.

00:09:08.010 --> 00:09:10.196
Catch you guys in the next one. Peace.

00:09:10.196 --> 00:09:13.029
(energetic music)

